DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Interval");

$set_ans_3 = Compute("[3, infinity) U ({-10, -6})");
$set_ans_4 = Compute("[3, infinity) U [3, infinity) U [3, infinity) U [3, infinity)");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("(7, infinity) U (7, infinity)");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("(7, infinity) U ((7, infinity)) U ((7, infinity) U {-8, -5, 5, 6, 7}) U ({-8, -5, 5, 6, 7})");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

What is the value of [`19+12-19+16/18`]? [_____]{answer=>Formula("12.8888888889"),width=>1}
---

What is the value of [`14+4-17+0/11`]? [_____]{Real(1.)}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-8, -5, 5, 6, 7\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x > 6\}`]

Compute:
- [`B \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`B \cup (B) \cup (B \cup A) \cup (A) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-10, -6\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x \geq 3\}`]

Compute:
- [`B \cup (A) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}
- [`B \cup B \cup B \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 8, 1, -4 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 2, 10, 8 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -9, -4, 5 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<8, 1, -4>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \vec{w} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-9, -4, 5>") . Compute("<8, 1, -4>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<2, 10, 8>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<8, 1, -4>"))}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<2, 10, 8>"))}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 10, -6, 3 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -4, 5, -3 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -3, -10, -3 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-4, 5, -3>") x Compute("<-3, -10, -3>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-4, 5, -3>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \vec{w} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-3, -10, -3>") . Compute("<10, -6, 3>")}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-4, 5, -3>") x Compute("<10, -6, 3>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<10, -6, 3>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-3, -10, -3>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
